#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""git-heat — walkable commit-decay heatmap for any git repo or subdirectory.

Per-path heat from git history with exponential *commit* decay, optional HTML
tree + syntax-highlighted file viewer, and a focus slider (half-life in commits).

Heat model
  raw = sum over non-initial touches of exp(-age / tau)
  tau = half_life / ln(2); age = commits behind HEAD (0 = HEAD)
  heat = 2 * (1 - exp(-1/tau)) * raw
    → touched every commit forever converges to ~2 at any half-life
  dir heat = max of non-noise leaves under it
  initial commit excluded; noise basenames (Cargo.toml, SOURCE_REV) → heat 0
    and do not contribute to parent directory max

Examples
  git-heat                          # CLI ranking for cwd's repo
  git-heat --serve                  # heatmap in-memory at http://127.0.0.1:8765/
  git-heat ~/src/arch/asf --html    # write git-heat.html only
  git-heat crates/codegen --serve   # one subdirectory
  git-heat --half-life 3 --top 20 .

See also: firmatum/utils/git-heat/README.md
"""

